      "dom_id": "question-72",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Solve the equation ${5}^{x}=\\frac{1}{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $\\frac{1}{5}$ as ${5}^{-1}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ {5}^{x} & ={5}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(5)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x} & ={5}^{-1} \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1.$",
