      "dom_id": "question-64060",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Solve the equation $3\\cdot {2}^{y}=24.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by dividing both sides by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot {2}^{y} & =24 \\\\ \\frac{3\\cdot {2}^{y}}{3} & =\\frac{24}{3} \\\\ {2}^{y} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite $8$ as ${2}^{3}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{y} & =8 \\\\ {2}^{y} & ={2}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(2)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{y} & ={2}^{3} \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=3.$",
